  "question": {
    "text": "Let the distance between two parallel lines be 5 units and a point $P$ lie between the lines at a unit distance from one of them. An equilateral triangle $P Q R$ is formed such that $Q$ lies on one of the parallel lines, while $R$ lies on the other. Then $(Q R)^2$ is equal to _______ -.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "28",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/QJQMvG1aD6ROk5-CofF9WFOO1f1uwIzSixEPH_iDDQM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$P R=\\operatorname{cosec} \\theta, P Q=4 \\sec (30+\\theta)$\n\nFor equilateral\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{d}=\\mathrm{PR}=\\mathrm{PQ} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\cos \\left(\\theta+30^{\\circ}\\right)=4 \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cos \\theta-\\frac{1}{2} \\sin \\theta=4 \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\tan \\theta=\\frac{1}{3 \\sqrt{3}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{QR}^2=\\mathrm{d}^2=\\operatorname{cosec}^2 \\theta=28\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
